From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: no tip to sign in to Chrome to save passwords

On a sign-in form, Chrome showed a tip next to its menu: "To save strong
passwords with Google Password Manager, sign in to Chrome". No one signs
in to Chrome on NickelOS (local accounts have no Google account, Chrome
0005), so the tip asked for something that isn't there. It is shown now
only to a profile signed in to Chrome, which NickelOS doesn't have: never.
Chrome still offers to save passwords on the device when one is entered.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/password_manager/chrome_password_manager_client.cc b/chrome/browser/password_manager/chrome_password_manager_client.cc
index 1e70841..0af7bf6 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/password_manager/chrome_password_manager_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/password_manager/chrome_password_manager_client.cc
@@ -2349,6 +2349,13 @@ void ChromePasswordManagerClient::MaybeShowSavePasswordPrimingPromo(
             IdentityManagerFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile())) {
       const bool signed_in =
           identity_manager->HasPrimaryAccount(signin::ConsentLevel::kSignin);
+      // NickelOS: no one signs in to Chrome (local accounts have no Google
+      // account), so the tip's other version, "sign in to Chrome" to save
+      // passwords with Google Password Manager, asked for something that
+      // isn't there. Passwords are saved on the device as before.
+      if (!signed_in) {
+        return;
+      }
       user_education::FeaturePromoParams params(
           feature_engagement::kIPHPasswordsSavePrimingPromoFeature);
       params.body_params = l10n_util::GetStringUTF16(
